{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-328066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/0eccac1629f5ab7d80fe4a7a6d4b1f58867adeed023e957f1f52daa885a745fa.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{UP}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{UT}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{RQ}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=$ \n {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-328066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $R$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=\\overset{\\to }{RP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/c3abc51a0c48faa7853eb2ef605412ca6311866994b15a579b7bc7e7db63ee15.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RP}=-d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=-a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/a53de4a8dcbd4a5d1f7640d5e1d4c8b6fd6e5e24388f432d279392727b11dd59.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{RP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =-d+(-a) \\\\  & =-d-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-328066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-328066" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-328066" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-d-a"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-328086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/6709c80eeddea3d31d68d51816a0249758d5a535eb5f2e6983f8e786faf3f227.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{QT}=$ \n {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-328086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/cd8dc0d2e01927c8b2ca116265b257d835a1baae62272b703610f2947d92a8c2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QS}=-b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{ST}=-c.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/8ed8c71e0d45ae0c9cf7d8a7d2889ee3a79471aaeb408ad0f53f487523daac13.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST} \\\\  & =-b+(-c) \\\\  & =-b-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-328086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-328086" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-328086" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-b-c"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-327824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/4290dec2be26edf6d3b12bf6ffb0fd69cfe9f672dbd02fd970c1bfc3e8c01c2a.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=d,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RS}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{RP}$ in terms of vectors $a,d,$ and $c.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $d,$ and $c.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{RP}=$  \n {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-327824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $R$ to $P$ consisting only of the vectors $a,d,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RP}=\\overset{\\to }{RQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/b6eb4bdf68dcecd124ec7129b94b6c5adccc826f505ecda653069640efa439e2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/90749b45c5e992ba17f09c6a3597adebcdad2ab9d354b2aee7e41058af69863a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RP} & =\\overset{\\to }{RQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP} \\\\  & =d+a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-327824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-327824" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-327824" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "d+a"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-275812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/3db9a8b3774e6d05efa1d3cbe262a16e2824f249c9fecfebf605ec8de7ca0634.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{AB}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{EB}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{EC}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DC}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{CB}$ in terms of vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{CB}=$    \n {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-275812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $C$ to $B$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EB},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/1c1826cfb7602c6380fed1e2aa3c380f575a29185c46ca969d212d94f7c11aed.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CE}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{EB}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/c013029af2f1d0dd727ac3c2dc701334fe51a9391b9691144a12f4cfff25c3d5.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB} & =\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EB} \\\\  & =-c+b \\\\  & =b-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-275812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-275812" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-275812" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "b-c"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-69531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/0236def5e17743a95be036e4f3c7b0dcf1a5c150ef53e56464f06afd6afcb5ca.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{QS}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{PT}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{QT}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{TS}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-69531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, \n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{TS}=\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PS},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/6d9225f220f50031fcbc7680c697b31eb8ce7733f07b83713c0dbe0c2ad89490.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{TP}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/533805fc0d558bde49590a6dd82414de22efeeadbc76e91760bea33bcd0ceeff.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TS} & =\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PS} \\\\  & =-c+a \\\\  & =a-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133