\to }{TP}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $P$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ \n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{TP}=\\overset{\\to }{TR}+\\overset{\\to }{RQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP}\n$$\n\n \n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/e0e6351dfbef6dadf6a6fb179f1545622ddaeab24c2c06dee03c87821304695c.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{TR}=-d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/02899ac9c536b0020514780db617e29977a5dc4daf60f42d80ed671883327fe3.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TP} & =\\overset{\\to }{TR}+\\overset{\\to }{RQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP} \\\\  & =-d+b+a \\\\  & =a+b-d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-143000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer