g to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QS}=\\overset{\\to }{QT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}+\\overset{\\to }{RS}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/2297c60ae34a641e498aa41346778e327fd2286657914272088ddb9f9b03bcb7.png)\n\n  \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TR}=c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{RS}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/fb4850a7d309448213c1ac5572dfe112555a2938790b24fad03ebb4669e3d95a.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QS} & =\\overset{\\to }{QT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}+\\overset{\\to }{RS} \\\\  & =a+c+b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-142998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-142998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-142998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=a+c+b"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=a+c+d"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=a+c-d"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=a-b-c"] ["ma