d these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/ff4b4292bb8a15551cb22da1f621684e9fdf24d35ae873b408dc612e5b3255e8.png)\n\n   \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QS} & =\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR}+\\overset{\\to }{RS} \\\\  & =a-d+b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-141480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-141480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-141480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=a+b+c"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=a-b+c"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=a-d+b"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=b+d+c"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=c-d+b"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-141480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{QS}=a-d+b"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-335826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/4ad1c49955142936f8b6fef257af8021e4eb9aa576cd37ebed149e5a31fbedc8.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{EF}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{GE}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{AF}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{GC}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ in terms of  $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{AC}=$   \n {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-335826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $A$ to $C$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AC}=\\overset{\\to }{AF}+\\overset{\\to }{FE}+\\overset{\\to }{EG}+\\overset{\\to }{GC}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/e24ac0b6cf4f039cd1e8b2e1aa5dd921ea637fb2fe46666a0091372dfce87d44.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AF}=c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{FE}=-a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{EG}=-b\\,\\overset{\\to }{GC}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/37c3758dc7a4c8a5b79c3e687e77f62090282410e3bf45bfade3494cd3b8055b.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AC} & =\\overset{\\to }{AF}+\\overset{\\to }{FE}+\\overset{\\to }{EG}+\\overset{\\to }{GC} \\\\  & =c+(-a)+(-b)+d \\\\  & =c-a-b+d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-335826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-335826" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-335826" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "c-a-b+d"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-277042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/241d4b1d29efddc5a9feb13b835d0caab6af354d3f62387dc92d14ff81942a6d.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{UP}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{UT}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{RP}$ in terms of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{RP}=$   \n {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-277042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $R$ to $P$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RP}=\\overset{\\to }{RT}+\\overset{\\to }{TU}+\\overset{\\to }{UP}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/b4ebdca78235f8f82564db1821320c7bb886447cb012813173e9c50558dbc9bb.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RT}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TU}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TU}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/540f94306cc497d87dc1f15d61ea929e042944f7c6f711a2bcf6b1f944c48228.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RP} & =\\overset{\\to }{RT}+\\overset{\\to }{TU}+\\overset{\\to }{UP} \\\\  & =d-c+b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-277042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-277042" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-277042" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "d-c+b"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/86aac25c634d29639329ae53209141ce81a3a82a70d42a4c2dfc6d356ee378b8.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DB}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{CD}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB} & =(\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC})+\\overset{\\to }{CB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA})+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =(\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC})+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/15f4bd7f8ecf8f61ce84858e33cdfa468b0de360fac19b0713b6b2dbc4af8d2e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Equality I is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF} & =\\overset{\\to }{AB}+\\overset{\\to }{FA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FB} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA} & =\\overset{\\to }{DE}+(\\overset{\\to }{EA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BE}+\\overset{\\to }{ED})+\\overset{\\to }{DC} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}+\\overset{\\to }{DC} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BC} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{CB}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/e17584d96cb8d83ccb1abfbd16c4117f58639b7cd3462ee50ad3f31e4eabe279.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}=\\overset{\\to }{BD}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{FC}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Equality I is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC} & =\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+(\\overset{\\to }{AE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =(\\overset{\\to }{CD}+\\overset{\\to }{DE})+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CF} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{FC}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0b