ned}\\overset{\\to }{FA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA} & =\\overset{\\to }{FA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FB} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BF}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CF} & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-69538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-69538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-69538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-69538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/67706db50684aef52269d20065caa21e4301834835e10e1fd3e456646ae2b32e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DF}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} & =(\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB})+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB} & =\\overset{\\to }{FB}+\\overset{\\to }{BD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "c81ed246ba7e02f78a535ec314ca133f82625b44c0bf6754dcb30eb9e3f81e5d"} {"question" "e-9934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/7431bd3281e4e49f4caaa5b701885fb64c58196b2256af9d8744decd9a0d0793.png)\n\n  \n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overrightarrow{PS}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{b},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{c},$ and $\\overrightarrow{TS}=\\mathbf{d}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TQ}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c},$ and $\\mathbf{d}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-9934.json" "file_sha256" "980d5d85295de79349e3057d120ad549a606bddca39784d13a79ea2c577e648b"} {"question" "e-9934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b, \\mathbf c,$ and $\\mathbf d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TQ}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/4902397acd28e2e5f85063ba55c576d3768360225a705f31a66bd460405dd5a6.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TS}} = \\mathbf{d}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}} = -\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/08086f7e09568f908aa4919a1156d52e465216221be8908e72a1fd90ec8843dd.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{TS}+\\overset{\\to }{SQ} \\\\  & =d+(-b) \\\\  & =d-b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-9934.json" "file_sha256" "980d5d85295de79349e3057d120ad549a606bddca39784d13a79ea2c577e648b"} {"question" "e-4277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the diagram shown below, where $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{c}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TS}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/04ce04bf7c7f88d6578c74db0d7398a6d299d11bd9f60f4fc4b6e1bfb0129f3b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-4277.json" "file_sha256" "30b59dc93766fdd2a22ab2a54b4bcd67d6b37f48fa86353c4e816e9f4a8b420f"} {"question" "e-4277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b,$ or $\\mathbf c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TP}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{PQ}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{QS}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/53940607b5cbf0220008e6e31ec60f2fd7fd2e4f70c5a8e95e7fcfd64064b095.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TP}} = -\\mathbf{b}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{PQ}} = \\mathbf{a}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{QS}} = \\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/810cce10eb330b1767a101d9107a9534c437daa123f13056a486a9fc96dbab89.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TS} & =\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QS} \\\\  & =-b+a+c \\\\  & =a-b+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-4277.json" "file_sha256" "30b59dc93766fdd2a22ab2a54b4bcd67d6b37f48fa86353c4e816e9f4a8b420f"} {"question" "e-5015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/2420154d44b786c6aad54212760e9a37ce67dbdce94a7043039f0e824c5ef9bc.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}-\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AC}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{DC}=\\overrightarrow{BA}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-5015.json" "file_sha256" "5e2f3809db124f9f2c6722505298a9e6cb42989f1a852460de9e2d244b297aa8"} {"question" "e-5015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Equality I is true. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}.$\n\n- Equality II is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB}-\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CA} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{AC}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nsince $\\overrightarrow{CA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ have opposite directions.\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{DC}\\neq\\overrightarrow{BA}$ since they have opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-5015.json" "file_sha256" "5e2f3809db124f9f2c6722505298a9e6cb42989f1a852460de9e2d244b297aa8"}] "usage" {"e-5015" [] "e-9934" [] "q-69538" [] "e-4277" []} "basis" 1477 "retractions" [[17592186097260 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/q-69538.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCEF$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $BF^(→)$?\n\n1. $BC^(→) + CE^(→) + EF^(→)$\n2. $FA^(→) - BA^(→)$\n3. $BC^(→) + CF^(→)$"] [17592186096524 :question/problem "Consider the diagram above, where $\\overrightarrow{PS}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{b}$, $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{c}$, and $\\overrightarrow{TS}=\\mathbf{d}$. Find $\\overrightarrow{TQ}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c}$, and $\\mathbf{d}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/e1428d48e9b657cb65b4abaf82ef8e51.png)"] [17592186096524 :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b, \\mathbf c$, and $\\mathbf d$.\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TQ}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/d79b0f30be6e0809efe831e4862b1043.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TS}} = \\mathbf{d}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}} = -\\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/20b51829636015f084208e464d30bea9.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nTQ^(→) &= TS^(→) + SQ^(→) \\\\\n&= d + (-b) \\\\\n&= d - b\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096367 :question/problem "Consider the diagram shown below, where $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{c}$. Find $\\overrightarrow{TS}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/ee9aee4946e062b8a7ad1fae2e350d37.png)"] [17592186096367 :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b$, or $\\mathbf c$.\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TP}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{PQ}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{QS}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/70335ddb9f1d79ca14b9138a4291465d.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TP}} = -\\mathbf{b}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{PQ}} = \\mathbf{a}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{QS}} = \\mathbf{c}\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/f5c06f75325a6ca44c7da008f6706fb2.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nTS^(→) &= TP^(→) + PQ^(→) + QS^(→) \\\\\n&=-b + a + c \\\\\n&= a - b + c\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096409 :question/problem "In parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1102/Source/Images/38d6af513afb9edf4208166303e35ed3.png)\n\n1. $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$\n2. $\\overrightarrow{CB}-\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AC}$\n3. $\\overrightarrow{DC}=\\overrightarrow{BA}$"] [17592186096409 :question/worked-solution "- Equality I is true. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$.\n- Equality II is false. Indeed,\n$CB^(→) - AB^(→)|= CB^(→) + BA^(→); = CA^(→); \\ne AC^(→)$\nsince $\\overrightarrow{CA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ have opposite directions.\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{DC}\\neq\\overrightarrow{BA}$ since they have opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""]] "immutable_answers" [17592186095918 17592186095919 17592186095920 17592186095921 17592186095922] "immutable_fields" [[17592186095917 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095917 :answer-field/id] [17592186095917 :answer-field/key] [17592186095917 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
